# --- Cooldown Manager (downport of NewEra/CooldownViewer) — PHASE 1: Essential + Utility ---
# Retail's Cooldown Manager runs on C_CooldownViewer, which exists on no Classic-family client;
# NewEra rebuilt it as retail's visual model over curated per-class data, and that is what ports.
# Load order: ClassData (pure tables) -> CooldownViewer (core: settings store, spell-list
# resolution) -> ItemMixins (the per-tile mixin) -> Viewers (frames built in Lua, replacing
# CooldownViewer.xml — MaskTexture and GridLayoutFrame are both unavailable here) -> Register
# (movers + options tab, replacing EditModeRegister.lua). See modules/cooldownviewer/PORT_PLAN.md.
modules\cooldownviewer\ClassData.lua
# WotLK seed: additive appends onto the vanilla lists above, plus the whole of Death Knight. Every
# id is generated from this client's own Spell.dbc + SkillLineAbility.dbc, never hand-typed.
# Must load AFTER ClassData (it appends to those tables) and BEFORE the viewer core reads them.
modules\cooldownviewer\CdmSeedWotLK.lua
# Phase 7d: the per-class catalog of trackable SELF-BUFFS — what the Tracked Buffs/Bars picker
# OFFERS, standing in for retail's curated per-spec aura set. Also generated from this client's own
# data (tools/cdm-spellgen/gen_auracatalog.py), and read by CooldownViewer's catalog accessor.
modules\cooldownviewer\CdmAuraCatalog.lua
modules\cooldownviewer\CooldownViewer.lua
# Phase 8a: the VIEWERS' art (the /cdm window's own is SettingsAssets.lua, far below). Must load
# before ItemMixins/AuraItemMixins, whose OnLoad resolves these atlases as each tile is built.
modules\cooldownviewer\Assets.lua
# On-use trinket discovery + the per-token assignment registry. Overrides CooldownViewer.lua's
# GetEquipItemsForCategory fallback, so it must load after it and before Viewers reads it.
modules\cooldownviewer\Equip.lua
modules\cooldownviewer\ItemMixins.lua
modules\cooldownviewer\Viewers.lua
# Phase 3, the aura-driven viewers. AuraItemMixins needs M.CropIcon/M.TooltipSetSpell from
# ItemMixins; BuffViewers needs M.BaseViewerMixin from Viewers — so both load after those two.
modules\cooldownviewer\AuraItemMixins.lua
modules\cooldownviewer\BuffViewers.lua
# Phase 4a: per-cooldown alerts and ready sounds. The ENGINE and its stores only — assignment UI
# belongs to the Phase 4b settings panel. AlertData is generated
# (tools/cdm-spellgen/gen_alertdata.py) and must precede Alerts, which reads it.
modules\cooldownviewer\AlertData.lua
modules\cooldownviewer\SoundAlertData.lua
modules\cooldownviewer\Alerts.lua
# Phase 4b-1: the standalone /cdm settings window (shell). SettingsAssets registers the side-tab
# art and must load before the panel builds tabs from it. Both need core/Tabs.lua and
# core/PanelChrome.lua, which load far earlier.
modules\cooldownviewer\SettingsAssets.lua
modules\cooldownviewer\SettingsPanel.lua
# 4b-2: the category model and the grids that render it. CdmArsenal is generated
# (tools/cdm-spellgen/gen_arsenal.py) and feeds the adapter's Hidden catalog, so it loads first;
# SettingsCategories replaces the panel's RefreshLayout stub, so it loads after the panel.
modules\cooldownviewer\CdmArsenal.lua
modules\cooldownviewer\SettingsAdapter.lua
modules\cooldownviewer\SettingsCategories.lua
# 4b-3: the right-click item menu and the settings cog — the assignment surface that finally makes
# the Phase 4a alert and ready-sound stores reachable. Needs core/Menu.lua and CDS.adapter.
modules\cooldownviewer\SettingsMenu.lua
# 4b-4: drag to reorder and reassign. Needs the adapter's ReorderTo/AssignAt and the tiles built by
# SettingsCategories, which supplies the OnDragStart that calls in here.
modules\cooldownviewer\SettingsReorder.lua
# 4b-5: named layouts, import/export, and the snapshot/restore pair that finally makes the panel's
# Revert button real. Needs core/Menu.lua for the footer menu and CDS.RefreshLayout from
# SettingsCategories, so it loads last of the settings files.
modules\cooldownviewer\SettingsPresets.lua
# 4c: the Settings tab. SettingsControls is the widget kit (checkbox / slider / menu-button over the
# client's own templates, since DragonUI's AceGUI option controls only render inside an AceGUI
# container); SettingsOptions is the page it builds. The page reads M.VIEWER_SPECS, which Register.lua
# defines below — that is fine, it is read when the tab is first opened, not at load.
modules\cooldownviewer\SettingsControls.lua
modules\cooldownviewer\SettingsOptions.lua
# Each viewer's own settings as a dialog beside the frame in edit mode, retail's shape.
# Needs the SettingsControls kit above and NE.RegisterHUDFrame's `editorSettings` seam; Register.lua
# below hands it one opener per viewer at PLAYER_LOGIN.
modules\cooldownviewer\EditorPanel.lua
modules\cooldownviewer\Register.lua

# --- Level Up Display (retail's level-up banner, learned from the live server) ---
# Rebuild rather than a port. Both prior versions ship a hand-typed spellList[CLASS][level] table
# that is only correct for the server it was written against; this addon runs on many. Harvest.lua
# reads the same facts off the trainer window (GetTrainerServiceInfo / ...LevelReq / ...Icon),
# battleground brackets (GetBattlegroundInfo) and the client's dungeon lists (GetLFGDungeonInfo)
# instead, so a custom server's own abilities and levels are picked up without any baked data.
# Load order: Assets (art + entry-type presets) -> Data (the small Blizzlike fallback for what no
# API reports) -> Harvest (writes the store) -> Unlocks (merges observed over fallback; reads both
# of the above) -> Banner + SideDisplay (the two views, both call Unlocks) -> Register (events,
# options, mover, /nelevelup).
modules\levelup\Assets.lua
modules\levelup\Data.lua
modules\levelup\Harvest.lua
modules\levelup\Unlocks.lua
modules\levelup\Banner.lua
modules\levelup\SideDisplay.lua
modules\levelup\Register.lua

